120 - There's a Song in the Air
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 120
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[G]There’s a song in the [D7]air!
There’s a [G]star in the [D7]sky!
There’s a [G]mother’s [Gm]deep [D]prayer
And a [A7]baby’s low [D]cry!
[D7]And the [G]star rains its fire
while the [D7]beautiful sing,
For the [G7]manger of [Am]Bethle[Cm]hem
[D7]cradles a [G]King!

Verse 2:
[G]There's a [D7]tumult of joy
[G]O'er the [D7]wonderful birth,
[G]For [Gm]the virgin's [D]sweet boy
[A7]Is the Lord [D]of the earth.
[D7]Aye! the star [G]rains its fire
[D7]while the beautiful sing,
[G7]For [Am]the manger [Cm]of Bethlehem
[D7]cradles [G]a King!

Verse 3:
[G]In the light [D7]of that star
[G]Lie the [D7]ages impearled;
[G]And [Gm]that song [D]from afar
[A7]Has swept [D]over the world.
[D7]Every hearth [G]is aflame
[D7]and the beautiful sing
[G7]In the [Am]homes of [Cm]the nations
[D7]that Jesus [G]is King!

Verse 4:
[G]We rejoice [D7]in the light,
[G]And we [D7]echo the song
[G]That comes [Gm]down through [D]the night
[A7]From the [D]heavenly throng.
[D7]Aye! we shout to [G]the lovely evangel they bring,
[D7]And we greet in His cradle
[G7]our [Am]Savior [Cm]and King!
